── UNKNOWN NAME ────────────────────────────── E0211_c_int_type.lt:1:13  [E0211]

Stilt's integer type is `i64`, not `int`:

  1 │ fn twice(n: int) -> i64 { n * 2 }
    │             ^^^

Stilt's primitive types are written in lower case, as `i64`, `f64`, `bool` and
`str`.

To fix it, write `i64`:

  1 │ fn twice(n: i64) -> i64 { n * 2 }
    │             ~~~
